{
  "title": "The Missing Layer",
  "says": "A busy board for the browser. Every knob is something this tab can already do.",
  "what": "The site holds no application and no data. It gives a grammar, and each browser that opens it is one live state. This file is the whole board: the one script on the site is a generator that reads it and turns the shapes it knows into running code.",
  "rule": "The board is one screen: no scroll, no navigation. The page the loaded JSONs make may scroll. On load only the title and one line are visible. No text is ever run as code; the page asks the browser to refuse it. Only shapes the generator knows become code.",
  "screen": {
    "width": 1280,
    "height": 800
  },
  "doors": {
    "cover": "The page opens on a title and one line. The word explore in the line leads to /explore. The board is built behind it. Touch the title to go in, or call board.enter().",
    "knobs": "Touch a store, touch a verb, type into Name and Value, touch Do. Undo takes back the last thing done.",
    "shape": "Type or paste JSON into Shape and touch Generate. A shape is one of: a run {\"store\", \"verb\", \"Name\", \"Value\"}; bare steps {\"steps\": [...]}; a list of shapes; or a whole contract like this file, which rebuilds the board.",
    "round trip": "Everything that runs is listed under Ran as the shape it was, with the code it stood for. Touch a line to put it back in Shape, or touch Hand back for all of it in order, then Generate.",
    "floppy": "Save downloads what the board is and holds as plain JSON; Load takes the files back and rebuilds it. The same through Shape: {\"keep\": true} writes the floppies into Shape, {\"keep\": {\"size\": 4000}} makes each at most that many bytes, and Generate takes them back, in any order. A floppy holds records: the board, each store, each thing held. It never holds code; the generator rebuilds from the records. From a script: board.serialize(size) and board.deserialize(floppies). By address: /serialize downloads the floppies; /deserialize asks whether to download a copy first, then takes the files. Rebuilding wipes everything first: the site goes back to the board it shipped with, every kept store empty, and is then rebuilt from the floppies.",
    "matrix": "The site ships JSONs beside the board; \"ships\" names them. Each has an id of two levels and brings named things, each a list of steps, and may bring stores and parts. Through Shape: {\"load\": \"email.wire\"} loads one from the site, a JSON pasted whole loads itself, {\"unload\": \"email.wire\"} takes one out. Nothing runs because it was loaded: each time the loaded set changes, the page is drawn again from all of it in the order of the addresses, so any order of loading gives the same page. Every thing gets its place and its address, like email.wire.inbox. What waits on something that is not loaded says so and does nothing; that part is the reader's. Page shows what the loaded JSONs make; Board comes back. A reload forgets what was loaded; what the stores hold stays. A floppy carries the loaded JSONs with everything else."
  },
  "addresses": {
    "/": "The cover: a title and one line, whose word explore leads to /explore. The board is behind it.",
    "/explore": "The whole field of interaction on one page: every door, address, script call, store and verb, and the grammar, written out from this file.",
    "/serialize": "Downloads what the board is and holds, as floppies.",
    "/deserialize": "Asks whether to download a copy first, then takes floppies, wipes everything and rebuilds.",
    "/contract.json": "This file.",
    "/email/wire.json": "A shipped JSON: the id email.wire is the file email/wire.json. The dot is the folder."
  },
  "ships": {
    "email.wire": "The wireframe of an email with an inbox and a sent box, and its two stores, email.wire.inbox and email.wire.sent. Alone: every layout, one after the other, with its id.",
    "email.touch": "The interaction of that email. With the wireframe: one layout at a time, compose opens, send sends, a row opens.",
    "email.stub": "A stub on the other end: ten seconds after a mail is sent it answers. Unloaded, nothing answers, and the reader answers through Shape: {\"store\": \"email.wire.inbox\", \"verb\": \"put\", \"Name\": the subject, \"Value\": the answer}."
  },
  "script": {
    "board.enter()": "Shows the board.",
    "board.serialize(size)": "Gives the floppies as a list of JSON texts; size is the most bytes on each, 1474560 if left out.",
    "board.deserialize(floppies)": "Takes floppies back, as text or parsed, one or many, in any order; wipes everything and rebuilds when the set is whole. Does not ask first.",
    "board.engine": "The engine number written on every floppy.",
    "the DOM": "The board's buttons and fields are in the page from load and can be operated without showing it.",
    "board.load(id or JSON)": "Loads a shipped JSON by its id, or a JSON handed whole.",
    "board.unload(id)": "Takes a loaded JSON out.",
    "board.loaded()": "The ids of what is loaded.",
    "board.page()": "Shows the page the loaded JSONs make."
  },
  "grammar": {
    "from": "start at one of: document, box, localStorage, sessionStorage, indexedDB, cookieStore, caches, history, location",
    "call": "call a method on the current thing; \"with\" lists what is passed",
    "get": "read a property of the current thing",
    "set": "write a property of the current thing; \"to\" is the value",
    "new": "make a Response or a URL; \"with\" lists what is passed",
    "as": "give the current thing a name; \"$name\" passes it later",
    "use": "go back to a named thing",
    "part": "run a named list of steps from \"parts\"",
    "entries": "turn the current thing into name and value pairs",
    "each": "run steps on every member of the current list",
    "gather": "run several lists of steps and keep each result under its own name",
    "words": "{Name} and {Value} are filled from the run; {Name:uri} makes it safe in an address; {Value:before=} and {Value:after=} split at the first equals sign",
    "keep": "on a store: how it is kept on a floppy. \"empty\" is the shape that empties it; \"each\" is the shape that puts one thing back, with {name} and {value} filled from the record. A store that holds elements needs only \"empty\". A store with no \"keep\" is not kept.",
    "touched": "wait for a touch on the thing at an address; \"then\" lists the steps, which start at that thing, and \"$touched\" is what was touched inside it",
    "changed": "wait for the store at an address to hold something else than it did; \"then\" lists the steps. The generator looks after everything it runs itself, so a write that does not come through it is not seen",
    "after": "wait a time in milliseconds; \"then\" lists the steps, which keep the current thing and every name as they were",
    "here": "in a thing of a loaded JSON, {\"use\": \"here\"} goes back to the thing's own place on the page"
  },
  "parts": {
    "thing": [
      {
        "from": "document"
      },
      {
        "call": "getElementById",
        "with": [
          "{Name}"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "things": [
      {
        "from": "indexedDB"
      },
      {
        "call": "open",
        "with": [
          "board",
          1
        ],
        "upgrade": [
          {
            "call": "createObjectStore",
            "with": [
              "things",
              {
                "keyPath": "name"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "call": "transaction",
        "with": [
          "things",
          "readwrite"
        ]
      },
      {
        "call": "objectStore",
        "with": [
          "things"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "shelf": [
      {
        "from": "caches"
      },
      {
        "call": "open",
        "with": [
          "board"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
